<BaseLayout title="Privacy and Local Processing" description="What stays on your device, how saved settings work and what ordinary website requests involve." noindex activeNav="/about/">
  <section class="legal-hero legal-shell"><p class="eyebrow">SELLER OPERATIONS LAB</p><h1>Privacy and local processing</h1></section>
  <section class="legal-content legal-shell">
    <p>Updated September 22, 2026.</p>
    <h2>Selected files</h2><p>The Image Prep workspace processes selected files in your browser. It does not upload them to Seller Operations Lab or store them in a server-side image library. There is no account or cloud synchronization.</p>
    <h2>Saved settings</h2><p>Saving is optional. Image settings and filename preferences may be stored in this browser's local storage. Photos and source image bytes are not stored there. Use “Forget saved settings” to remove the saved recipe.</p>
    <h2>Ordinary website requests</h2><p>Loading the site involves network requests. Cloudflare, our hosting provider, may process connection and security information such as IP addresses, requested URLs and request times. Local image processing does not mean every website visit is anonymous. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Advertising and analytics</h2><p>This release does not load advertising or analytics scripts. If advertising or analytics is enabled later, this policy and any applicable consent controls must be updated before those scripts run.</p>
    <h2>External links and contact</h2><p>Marketplace documentation and GitHub open services with their own privacy practices. GitHub issue reports are public; do not post images, personal details or confidential business information. <a href="/contact/">Contact and corrections</a>.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
